-> NOT a 401: the new apiGuestCheck guard did not turn away a valid authenticated caller.
-> No 'error'/'line' keys, no raw exception text in the body (global exception renderer masks it).
-> The 500 itself is the PRE-EXISTING, unrelated named-args bug in TaxController::getCalculateTax's
   call into CalculateTaxService::getCalculatedTax (categoryIds/quantity/addonQuantity/addonCategoryIds
   not declared by the service signature) — confirmed by both engineer + security reviewer during
   build/review, untouched by this diff, zero live callers of this route exist today. Correlated in
   storage/logs/laravel.log:
[2026-09-11 12:11:49] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Unknown named parameter $categoryIds {"trace_id":"54781ff7c727384a8fb0d06698606582","correlation_id":"b87fa505-1b87-434c-a6d5-ba9a363ac845","type":"Error","endpoint":"/api/v1/taxvat/get-calculated-tax"}

